= The Chronicle Closes

More than two years have passed since DuFour left office, and the Commonwealth has settled, uneasily, into what it is now to be. The crises that defined the age have burned down. The quarrels that remain belong to a different generation and a different chronicle.

The story of the republic's hardest years is told. What the Marchers made of them, and what was made of the Marchers, is now a matter for the histories.

- @game_over_1934: Bring the era to a close.
